07 — Tailscale Setup

What is this for?
Tailscale creates a private VPN mesh network between all your devices. It allows you to securely access your homelab services (like Navidrome) from anywhere without opening ports on your router or setting up a traditional VPN. Each device gets a stable 100.x.x.x IP address that works regardless of location.

Prerequisites
A free Tailscale account — sign up at https://tailscale.com
The Ubuntu Server VM (running Navidrome) is up and accessible on your local network

Installing Tailscale on the Ubuntu Server VM
SSH into your Ubuntu Server VM and run:

   curl -fsSL https://tailscale.com/install.sh | sh

Start Tailscale and authenticate:

   sudo tailscale up

A URL will appear in the terminal — open it in your browser and log in to your Tailscale account to authorize the machine.

Get the VM's Tailscale IP:

   tailscale ip -4

It will return a 100.x.x.x address — note this down, you will use it to connect remotely.

Enable Tailscale to Start on Boot

   sudo systemctl enable tailscaled

Installing Tailscale on Your iPhone
Install Tailscale from the App Store
Open the app and sign in with the same account you used above
Tap the toggle to connect
Your phone is now on the same private network as your homelab

Installing Tailscale on Your Computer (Optional)
Download from https://tailscale.com/download
Install and sign in with the same account
Your computer will also be able to reach 100.x.x.x addresses

Verify Devices Are Connected
In a browser go to https://login.tailscale.com/admin/machines
You should see all your connected devices listed with their 100.x.x.x addresses
All devices on the same Tailscale account can reach each other regardless of physical location

Accessing Navidrome Remotely
Once Tailscale is running on both the Ubuntu Server VM and your iPhone, open Substreamer and use the Tailscale IP instead of your local IP:

   Server URL    http://100.x.x.x:4533

Replace 100.x.x.x with the Tailscale IP of your Ubuntu Server VM (from the tailscale ip -4 command above).

This works over cellular data or any Wi-Fi network — Tailscale handles routing automatically.

How it Works
Without Tailscale    You would need to open a port on your router and expose Navidrome to the internet
With Tailscale       Traffic stays private within your Tailscale network, nothing is exposed publicly

